				<wikidot:authorName>TheMightyMcB</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4483018</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>See Incident Protocol 149-DE</p> </blockquote> <p>Yeah, see this is where you lost me for good. The fact that the conclusion of the SCP, the part where it all falls into place, is shoved in a tale that is completely separate from this piece is enough for my downvote alone. The era from which such a practice is deemed acceptable has long since passed. The entire <em>point</em> of an SCP is to tell a complete narrative within the restrictions of the format. I shouldn't have to go to a completely different <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Wikidot site</span> page (since the old addenda has now been localized here) to find your ending. This article doesn't stand on its own two feet.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
